  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**can** = poder / saber (hacer algo). Es igual para todas las personas y **no lleva -s**.",
      "",
      "| | Ejemplo |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| + | I can swim. · She can swim. |",
      "| − | I can't swim. (can't = cannot) |",
      "| ? | Can you swim? |",
      "",
      "**Respuestas cortas:** *Yes, I can. / No, I can't.*",
      "",
      "Después de *can* va el verbo en forma base: **sin *to***: *I can cook* (no *I can to cook*).",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *can* suena débil /kən/; *can't* suena fuerte y largo /kɑːnt/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "She cans swim.",
        "right": "She can swim.",
        "note": "Can no cambia ni lleva -s."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I can to swim.",
        "right": "I can swim.",
        "note": "Después de can no va to."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
